        "id": "ch17_6-1",
        "text": "Variables\nVariables are used in any programming language (not only in Python) to store\ntemporary data in memory. The main goal of a variable is to reuse it throughout\nthe source code.\nIn Python, we have multiple types of variables. The most common ones are\nthe following:\nI\nI Numbers : Will store digits\nI\nI Strings : Will store text\nI\nI Lists : Will store an array collection of values\nI\nI Tuples : Will store read-only array items\nI\nI Dictionaries : Will store key-value pairs\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Numbers\n\u2022 Arithmetic Operators\n\u2022 Strings\n\u2022 Lists\n\u2022 Tuples\n\u2022 Dictionary\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
